-- title:
--   Haar scaling of y ↦ σ(y) - ry on L ⊗_K Kᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, and write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $K$ and $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, equipped with a measurable-space structure that is the Borel structure of its topology, and let $\nu$ be an additive Haar measure on $E$. Let $r \in E$ be an element whose determinant norm $\mathrm{N}(r) = \mathrm{Algebra.norm}_{K_v}(r) \in K_v$ satisfies $\mathrm{N}(r) \neq 1$. Here [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaTensor`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L199) denotes the ring endomorphism $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$ of $E$ obtained from $\sigma$ and the identity of $K_v$. The assertion is that the pushforward of $\nu$ along the map $y \mapsto (\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(y) - r\,y$ equals the rescaling of $\nu$ by the non-negative real number $\|1 - \mathrm{N}(r)\|_{+}^{-1}$, the inverse of the norm of $1 - \mathrm{N}(r)$ computed in $K_v$.
--
--   This is the computation of the module (normalised determinant) of the $K_v$-linear map $y \mapsto \sigma(y) - r y$ on the semilocal algebra $L \otimes_K K_v$ for a cyclic extension $L/K$, in the special case of leading coefficient $1$: the Jacobian factor is $\|1 - \mathrm{N}(r)\|^{-1}$. It serves the analysis of twisted orbital integrals, being used in the estimate of integrals of automorphic forms against $\sigma$-twisted differences with a logarithmic trace term.
